  - m_Id: 315165939982336
    m_Localized: "<size=140%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Gunja Tteokbokki
      Kitchen Manual</font></size>\r\n<size=80%><color=#888888>\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500</color></size>\r\n\r\n<size=120%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">1. Kitchen Controls Basics</font></size>\r\nVeteran managers are faster
      with a keyboard than their hands! Mouse clicks work, but try learning the shortcuts
      below.\r\n\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Select Stove</font>:
      Press number keys <color=#87CEEB>1 ~ 5</color> to instantly select a stove
      to cook on.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Add Ingredients</font>:
      With a stove selected, press the keyboard to add ingredients.\r\n    - <color=#FFA500>Top
      Shelf (Q, W, E, R, T, Y, U)</color>: Base ingredients like Rice Cake, Fish
      Cake, Green Onion.\r\n    - <color=#FFA500>Middle Shelf (A, S, D, F, G, H,
      J)</color>: Various toppings like Sweet Potato, Egg, Ramen.\r\n    - <color=#FFA500>Bottom
      Shelf (Z, X, C, V, B, N, M)</color>: Various sauces that determine the menu's
      flavor.\r\n    <size=80%><Tip> For keys that are further away, hold <color=#87CEEB>Shift</color>
      to map them to closer keys.</size>\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Start Cooking</font>: Once all ingredients are added, press the <color=#87CEEB>Space
      Bar</color> to turn on the heat.\r\n\r\n<size=80%><color=#888888>\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500</color></size>\r\n\r\n<size=120%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">2. The Secret to Perfect Cooking</font></size>\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">The Absolute Basics</font>: Every Tteokbokki must include <color=#FF6347>Rice
      Cake x2, Fish Cake x2, Green Onion x1, Cabbage x1</color>, and <color=#FF6347>1
      Sauce</color>.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Menu Determination</font>:
      The final menu is decided by the sauce added along with the base ingredients.
      You cannot start cooking without a sauce.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Cooking Complete</font>: Once the heat is on and the gauge fills up,
      cooking is done. You can then drag the food to the packaging area.\r\n\r\n<size=80%><color=#888888>\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500</color></size>\r\n\r\n<size=120%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">3. Packaging & Delivery</font></size>\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Packaging</font>: Drag a finished wok to a packaging slot to neatly pack
      it into a delivery container.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Stacking
      System</font>: You can stack up to <color=#87CEEB>3</color> containers in a
      single packaging slot.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Delivery
      Complete</font>: Drag a receipt from the right side of the screen onto the
      packaged food to send it out for delivery.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Strict Evaluation</font>: The requested menu and <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Extra Ingredients (Toppings)</font> must perfectly match the receipt
      to succeed.\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Delivery Failure</font>:
      If you deliver the wrong food, you won't earn any money, and you might get
      a complaint call right away!\r\n\r\n<size=80%><color=#888888>\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500</color></size>\r\n\r\n<size=120%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">4. Essential Operations for the Manager</font></size>\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Emergency Early Closing</font>: If you run out of any base ingredient,
      or if all sauces are depleted, the shop will be forced to close. Always check
      your stock!\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Complaint Calls</font>:
      If you take too long to process an order or deliver the wrong food, the phone
      will ring. Answer it quickly, or you'll have to listen to the customer complain
      for even longer!\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Trash Bin</font>:
      If you make a mistake while adding ingredients or cook the wrong food, you
      can throw it in the trash bin. The same goes for receipts\u2014cancel unmanageable
      orders early!\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Closing & Taxes</font>:
      When business ends, you must pay taxes on the money you earned today. Don't
      forget to account for taxes when calculating your profit!\r\n\u25B6 <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Tomorrow's Bonus</font>: At closing, 2 bonus ingredients for the next
      day are announced. Selling food with these ingredients earns you an extra <color=#FF6347>\u20A95,000</color>
      per ingredient.\r\n\r\n<size=80%><color=#888888>\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500</color></size>\r\n\r\n<size=125%><font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\"><color=#32CD32>Veteran Manager's Secret Tips</color></font></size>\r\n1.
      <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Click the Receipts!</font>: Click a receipt
      on the right to see the total number of required ingredients at a glance. Look
      at the list and use shortcuts to add ingredients quickly.\r\n2. <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold
      SDF\">Use the Magnifying Glass</font>: Hover your mouse over cooked food to
      check its ingredients. Compare it with the receipt to deliver without mistakes.\r\n3.
      <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">Shop Convenience</font>: In the shop
      after closing, use the <color=#87CEEB>'1 of Low Stock'</color> button to easily
      restock. However, you can only order up to <color=#FF6347>3 sets</color> of
      each ingredient at a time.\r\n4. <font=\"KimjungchulMyungjo-Bold SDF\">The
      Secret of the Queue</font>: Don't panic if the receipt line is full. There
      are pending orders waiting in line out of sight. Once you complete one, the
      next order will appear immediately."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
